  server/
    http/              Fastify routes; thin — parse, authorize, call domain
    tasks/             task model + mutations (writes events in-transaction)
    auth/              sessions, current user
    events/            outbox: append(), claim(), markProcessed()
    notifications/
      interest.ts      interestedUsers(event) -> userId[]   ← the seam
      coalesce.ts      window logic: collapse same task+recipient
      dispatch.ts      creates deliveries, invokes adapters
      channels/
        in-app.ts      the one adapter in the slice
    worker/            polls outbox, drives coalesce -> dispatch
  db/                  SQLite schema + migrations

  Each notification module answers the three questions cleanly: [38;5;153minterest.ts[39m takes an event and returns user IDs (depends
  on the task/user read models only); [38;5;153mcoalesce.ts[39m takes pending deliveries and merges them (pure, depends on nothing);
  [38;5;153mdispatch.ts[39m writes deliveries and calls adapters (depends on the channel interface, not on any concrete channel). The
  adapter interface is one method, so adding email later touches [38;5;153mchannels/[39m and nothing else.

